# A random encounter in the hold, which needs nothing but walking for long
# enough. The battle system entered from the field rather than from a script.
name: encounter
summary: Walk the ship's hold for twenty minutes of game time until a fight starts.
frames: 30000
pad: 1600:start,1640:a,1800:start,1840:a,2000:start,2040:a,2200:start,2240:a
pad: 2400:start,2440:a,2600:start,2640:a,2800:start,2840:a,3000:start,3040:a
pad: 3200:start,3240:a
pad: 3600:a@150
pad: 15000:sup#1200,16500:sleft#600,18000:sup@900#400,19000:sright@1100#300
env: SOA_RENDER=1
env: SOA_SNAP=500
env: SOA_SPEED=3

shows: a battle entered from the field: the encounter transition, the battle
shows:   packages fetched from the ARAM cache a second time, and the return to
shows:   the same field map afterwards.
shows: whether the field keeps its footing over tens of thousands of frames.
shows:   build/boot_field.log mashed A from frame 14710 to 55360 without loading
shows:   anything new, which is what open-loop scripting looks like when it has
shows:   run out of reach (PLAN, track D).

evidence: docs/PROGRESS.md, "Three 25-minute mixed-input runs at triple speed:
evidence:   menus, random encounters, a game over and a restart from the title,
evidence:   no errors" -- build/boot_monkey2.log, boot_monkey3.log and
evidence:   boot_monkey4.log. Those are the runs that prove encounters happen
evidence:   under a script; this scenario is the cheap version of them.
evidence: build/boot_field.log for the hold itself (see hold.scn).

note: Whether an encounter lands inside this frame budget is what the run
note:   tells you, not something the checks assert: the encounter rate is the
note:   game's own, the guest clock is the host clock scaled (PLAN D4), and an
note:   invariant that depends on either would drift. The stick events are
note:   reconstructions for the reason hold.scn gives.
note: The first nine START/A pairs are the standard preamble: START at 1600
note:   dismisses the title, A at 1640 takes New Game, and the eight pairs that
note:   follow walk the first dialogue boxes. From 3600 one A press every 150
note:   frames advances everything after that. Every saved run in build/ that
note:   got past the title begins with exactly these nineteen events.
